{"parentUuid":"d445f444-3d7e-4da4-adba-a82d1bf65f11","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEks2ED3Ug7daCHk9svk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Since local assets share the app's origin, only remote https images pose a cross-origin problem. I'm planning to intercept response headers in main.mjs for image requests to https URLs, injecting a wildcard Access-Control-Allow-Origin header when one isn't already present.\n\nI should always override any existing ACAO header to \"*\" since a server-specified origin won't match app://local, and CORS mode should sidestep CORP restrictions for images too. On the renderer side, I need to add crossOrigin=\"anonymous\" to remote card images, likely via a shared helper exported from LiquidGlass.tsx.\n\nActually, I'm now second-guessing whether setting crossOrigin unconditionally on app:// windows is safe -- same-origin requests normally skip CORS checks, but I need to verify whether the app:// scheme is registered with CORS support, since Chromium only allows CORS-mode fetches for schemes explicitly marked as CORS-enabled in registerSchemesAsPrivileged.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1172,"cache_read_input_tokens":70292,"output_tokens":1144,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":997},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1172,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1144,"cache_read_input_tokens":70292,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1172,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1172},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDu