{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","id":"5f834962-2c72-4496-afe8-5b0a00a4d849","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:36:52.592Z","version":"2.1.305","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"a9ed8921dc21a185c51f032ab201ef86db193f2b4a3c27f0d2631dc37b2aa860","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"xhigh"}},"base":"debdd1a8-bae2-440c-a0d0-1f512bc8103f","keep":86,"tail":["d4656ed9f313a915dfd92260b1268a8755715c4ef5f4e1ff68f331191dee7c33","12776aa81e37bf6233cb8ac3376b297a82851e5665ebd670346b0f8c29210836","f2913525a3bf4135168fd9d8a4017a10de2f30088fb45d3dec42d60234dd6dad"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",88,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"ad8748a739e52b81648ddebb8cf2e4600c5a99153b191c5d34e3f71ad499b442"}
{"parentUuid":"a2c000ac-fd7d-42a9-9d50-1158648d8f92","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEmB3oEA657gAuFaVGzT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm working out that for the lens, the CSS shadow stays on the target element itself since the lens clips to its own glass, meaning I need a rule like `.item-zoom-pill.glass[data-liquid]` to preserve that glass shadow. I'm also noting that in lens mode, the small canvas inside the pill shouldn't contain the actual zoomed replica content directly.\n\nThe trickier issue is that in non-GPU fallback mode, the replica content sits as a direct DOM child of the wrapper, which would render unblurred on top of the pill's backdrop-filter glass since children paint above their own element's blur. So I need a CSS rule hiding that replica when it's a direct child of the lens wrapper, since in liquid mode the content actually gets moved inside the canvas instead and won't match that selector.\n\nThere's also a timing gap before the first GPU frame draws where the canvas is transparent but data-liquid hasn't been set yet — I think an undrawn WebGPU canvas renders as transparent, so the CSS glass can stay visible underneath without flashing during that gap.\n\nNow I need to work out replica positioning: the lens component renders a stage div with the zoomed image inside a LiquidGlass wrapper targeting the pill, and I need a layout effect that recalculates rects every render to align the dotted background — I'm figuring out how to get the pill's containing stage element to compute offsets correctly.\n\nI realize I should anchor coordinates using the wrapper's bounding rect as the canvas origin, then position the dotted stage background relative to that, matching the stage's actual border and background-origin behavior so the dots align exactly with the real stage.\n\nSince the lens sits inside the stage, I can just rely on CSS inheritance—defining a custom property on `.item-stage` for the background gradient, which the lens stage div can then reuse automatically without duplicating the gradient values.\n\nI'm also working out the lens image's position and sizing by computing its transformed bounding rect relative to the wrapper, and thinking through what triggers a stage re-render outside of normal React updates—window resize via ResizeObserver, and the stage inset transition when the inspector panel opens or closes.\n\nChecking whether the shadow beneath the unzoomed image could bleed under the pill when the image sits close to the stage bottom, since the shadow spread extends well past the image edge.\n\nI should give the lens image the same box-shadow as the stage image when unzoomed, then remove it once zoomed, so the darkened area under the pill matches correctly.\n\nActually I'm reconsidering the whole approach: instead of a replica image, maybe it's simpler to wrap the entire stage frame as the glass backdrop with the pill as the target, drawing the full displayed image through canvas. That avoids replica geometry but costs more GPU work per pan frame, since the full stage canvas (roughly 2MP) would need copying and the glass passes (blur, displacement, shadow) run across the whole canvas rather than just the lens area.\n\nBut I realize there's a bigger issue: during the flying-open animation, the stage inset changes every frame, which means the canvas would need to resize and reallocate each frame — that's expensive and risky for hitches, especially with large 6000px images. The lens approach sidesteps all of this, so I'll stick with it. Now I should trace back to find where ZoomableImage is called to understand its parent context.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9567,"cache_read_input_tokens":94745,"output_tokens":3390,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3076},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9567,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3390,"cache_read_input_tokens":94745,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9567,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9567},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":33883,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEmB3UNHzedzbZCPGKyZ","requestRef":"5f834962-2c72-4496-afe8-5b0a00a4d849","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"03b09034-76cc-47f3-a0ec-d389ff481fea","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:37:27.157Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"03b09034-76cc-47f3-a0ec-d389ff481fea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEmB3oEA657gAuFaVGzT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The zoom pill gets a small lens: a pill-sized canvas showing a thumbnail copy of what sits behind it. That keeps the item view, its open animation and the full-size image out of the canvas."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9567,"cache_read_input_tokens":94745,"output_tokens":3390,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3076},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9567,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3390,"cache_read_input_tokens":94745,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9567,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9567},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEmB3UNHzedzbZCPGKyZ","requestRef":"5f834962-2c72-4496-afe8-5b0a00a4d849","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6608f69b-6757-4ae5-8ec4-4ca7e03465aa","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:37:27.182Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
