{"parentUuid":"522d1eb6-ea3b-4d39-b6db-6438054cb3ce","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_012d25HifVZMYbnBYxYmvKcS","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d52ece4f-95db-4835-abbc-68b4dafff8ea","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:40:26.918Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"d52ece4f-95db-4835-abbc-68b4dafff8ea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEmRVPjehGP8ZYrsq1HD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm now setting up a performance probe script that records frame timing via requestAnimationFrame, tracking intervals between frames to measure cadence, though I note this continuous loop approach forces frames rather than measuring real rendering load.\n\nI'm weighing better measurement approaches: rAF deltas can show jank around 33ms+ versus a smooth 16.7ms vsync, but they only capture main-thread timing, not true GPU compositing cost -- LoAF (long-animation-frame) entries via PerformanceObserver could help but only flag frames over 50ms. I'm planning to drive synthetic mouse wheel scroll events through CDP at ~16ms intervals over the canvas grid while the rAF recorder collects timing data, then repeat the same test in CSS rendering mode for comparison.\n\nFor forcing CSS mode reliably without rebuilding, I realize command-line flag combinations may conflict, so instead I'll inject a script via CDP's addScriptToEvaluateOnNewDocument that deletes the layoutSubtree accessor off HTMLCanvasElement's prototype before the page loads, which should make the liquid glass support check fail and fall back to CSS -- letting me A/B test the same build with and without that injected script.\n\nFor measuring performance, mouse wheel events on the virtuoso grid scroller should trigger Chromium's native smooth-scroll animation per tick, which feels realistic enough to test with. I'm weighing whether to use chrome://tracing for GPU timing versus just counting paint events and rAF deltas during an idle period, and I'll start simple with rAF deltas plus paint counts rather than setting up full CDP Profiler tracing, while noting the Electron window size and display refresh rate as variables to account for.\n\nNow I'm writing perf.ts to capture these measurements.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3635,"cache_read_input_tokens":129606,"output_tokens":2768,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1204},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3635,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2768,"cache_read_input_tokens":129606,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3635},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":17686,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEmRV1BAwktdmgDkSZt4","requestRef":"a919ad70-1b85-4134-9717-4ade7ca39bb9","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b5f8e049-b1c4-431a-ab5f-bb0c282e31cc","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:40:26.917Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"b5f8e049-b1c4-431a-ab5f-bb0c282e31cc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEmRVPjehGP8ZYrsq1HD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now a perf A/B on the same build. Liquid mode is measured against CSS mode, which I force by hiding `layoutSubtree` before the page loads. Both runs do the same wheel scroll and sidebar toggle."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3635,"cache_read_input_tokens":129606,"output_tokens":2768,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1204},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3635,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2768,"cache_read_input_tokens":129606,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3635},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEmRV1BAwktdmgDkSZt4","requestRef":"a919ad70-1b85-4134-9717-4ade7ca39bb9","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a5201756-192c-4899-b849-6ccfcccf6f65","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:40:26.922Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"a5201756-192c-4899-b849-6ccfcccf6f65","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEmRVPjehGP8ZYrsq1HD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014S19WjjTQk929ZBx83v5CU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\liquid-glass-run\\perf.ts","content":"// bun perf.ts <port> <liquid|css>  — reloads the app in that mode, then measures\n// frame deltas while wheel-scrolling the grid and while toggling the sidebar,\n// and counts library canvas paints while idle.\nconst [portArg, mode] = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst list = await (await fetch(`http://127.0.0.1:${portArg}/json/list`)).json();\nconst page = list.find((t: { url: string; type: string }) => t.type === \"page\" && t.url.startsWith(\"app://\"));\nconst ws = new WebSocket(page.webSocketDebuggerUrl);\nawait new Promise((r) => ws.addEventListener(\"open\", r, { once: true }));\nlet id = 0;\nconst pending = new Map<number, (v: any) => void>();\nws.addEventListener(\"message\", (e) => {\n  const msg = JSON.parse(String(e.data));\n  if (msg.id && pending.has(msg.id)) { pending.get(msg.id)!(msg); pending.delete(msg.id); }\n});\nconst send = (method: string, params: object = {}) => new Promise<any>((r) => { const i = ++id; pending.set(i, r); ws.send(JSON.stringify({ id: i, method, params })); });\nconst evaluate = async (expression: string) => (await send(\"Runtime.evaluate\", { expression, awaitPromise: true, returnByValue: true })).result?.result?.value;\n\nconst injected = await send(\"Page.addScriptToEvaluateOnNewDocument\", {\n  source: mode === \"css\" ? \"delete HTMLCanvasElement.prototype.layoutSubtree;\" : \"\",\n});\nawait send(\"Page.reload\", {});\nawait Bun.sleep(3500);\nawait send(\"Page.removeScriptToEvaluateOnNewDocument\", { identifier: injected.result.identifier });\nconsole.log(mode, \"liquid targets:\", await evaluate(`document.querySelectorAll(\"[data-liquid]\").length`));\n\nconst recorder = `(() => { window.__d = []; window.__rec = true; let last = performance.now();\n  const f = (t) => { window.__d.push(t - last); last = t; if (window.__rec) requestAnimationFrame(f); };\n  requestAnimationFrame(f); })()`;\nconst stats = `(() => { window.__rec = false; const d = window.__d.slice(2).sort((a, b) => a - b);\n  const q = (p) => d[Math.min(d.length - 1, Math.floor(p * d.length))];\n  return { frames: d.length, median: +q(0.5).toFixed(1), p95: +q(0.95).toFixed(1), max: +d[d.length - 1].toFixed(1), over25ms: d.filter((x) => x > 25).length }; })()`;\n\n// Idle: paints on the library canvas with nothing happening.\nawait evaluate(`(() => { window.__paints = 0; document.querySelector(\".library-stage .liquid-glass-canvas\")?.addEventListener(\"paint\", () => window.__paints++); })()`);\nawait Bun.sleep(2000);\nconsole.log(\"idle paints in 2s:\", await evaluate(\"window.__paints\"));\n\n// Wheel scroll: 90 ticks, one every ~16ms, over the grid.\nawait evaluate(recorder);\nfor (let i = 0; i < 90; i++) {\n  await send(\"Input.dispatchMouseEvent\", { type: \"mouseWheel\", x: 760, y: 400, deltaX: 0, deltaY: i < 45 ? 120 : -120 });\n  await Bun.sleep(16);\n}\nawait Bun.sleep(600);\nconsole.log(\"scroll:\", JSON.stringify(await evaluate(stats)));\nconsole.log(\"paints during scroll:\", await evaluate(\"window.__paints\"));\n\n// Sidebar: collapse and reopen three times.\nawait evaluate(recorder);\nfor (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) {\n  await evaluate(`document.querySelector(\".edge-tab\").click()`);\n  await Bun.sleep(700);\n}\nconsole.log(\"sidebar:\", JSON.stringify(await evaluate(stats)));\nws.close();\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3635,"cache_read_input_tokens":129606,"output_tokens":2768,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1204},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":