{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","id":"7139d177-26ae-4f64-a452-2c869e6b60b3","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:43:58.739Z","version":"2.1.305","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"a9ed8921dc21a185c51f032ab201ef86db193f2b4a3c27f0d2631dc37b2aa860","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"xhigh"}},"base":"563974b7-0b9e-4d91-8473-2e51d4d8421c","keep":155,"tail":["b210447ba818abd8ec0d44b6316cd0c832bb20eb67b7807fa1435ce48948e558","481af267d2fedd19ce5886511da6cf7c841905f9fa043a6bbbca1a2348afdda4","7bc5a5ed5cd862d737a49bd7bf9fc5029defcfe19929ccfb0cac1a7e3dc3172a"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",157,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"5b73e7bcbb9049a2a1eb8dde5a69e98b7a1e1ce6fb10b7e657f7ebda646ad418"}
{"parentUuid":"4b63e92b-a39f-478a-9775-89ff055adc8b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEmiTphmnaDcTod48FPP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Running a real A/B test now: idle shows zero paints in both cases, and scroll performance is essentially equal, with a likely first-frame hitch from virtuoso or image decode. But the sidebar toggle reveals a clear regression—CSS has only 4 frames over 25ms (max 40-67ms) while liquid has 44 frames over 25ms with max times exceeding 200ms, confirming the predicted jank in liquid mode.\n\nFrame counts confirm it: CSS maintains roughly 624-630 frames over 4.2s while liquid drops to 478-496, losing about 130 frames. The expense comes from per-frame costs during resize—canvas dimension changes triggering swapchain reallocation, backdrop resizing causing the same content relayout as CSS, plus liquid-dom reallocating the html entry texture and all the WebGpuGlassCore render targets (blur textures etc.) sized to the canvas every frame, on top of copying the full content image to texture. The 200ms spikes suggest something even heavier is happening, like pipeline recreation or GPU sync stalls, so I'm considering whether to avoid resizing the canvas during the sidebar transition by fixing it to the maximum possible stage size, though the underlying content layout still needs to reflow to match the new width.\n\nStretching is ugly though, so instead maybe the canvas itself could cover the full window width always, with only the content host inside it resizing—so the sidebar animation becomes a layout-only change in the scroller's position, avoiding any texture reallocation during the transition.\n\nBut that risks the canvas visually overlapping the sidebar unless z-ordering is carefully managed, which feels fragile. A cheaper fallback would be to only ever grow the canvas's backing size and never shrink it mid-transition, allocating in discrete steps rather than every frame.\n\nRounding the canvas backing size to 256px buckets while keeping its CSS size clipped by an overflow-hidden wrapper means reallocations only happen when crossing a bucket boundary, not every frame. The inner content still lays out at the true stage size each frame, while the host/texture stays fixed at the bucketed size until it needs to grow.\n\nThe downside is extra GPU fill since the canvas can be up to ~255px larger than needed in each dimension, which could add noticeable cost during steady-state scrolling, so I'm wondering if bucket-sizing should only apply during transitions. I also suspect allocation isn't actually the real bottleneck -- it might be something else, like the WebGPU DOM content source recreating heavy state on resize, or costly work happening in the resize observer sync or surface resize calls.\n\nTo actually profile this, I'm thinking about instrumenting the paint pipeline directly: adding a capture-phase listener on an ancestor element to record the start time before the canvas's own paint listener runs, then a listener registered after the draw handler to record the end time, letting me measure the real main-thread cost of the draw handler during sidebar toggles.\n\nI also realize the content source adds its own paint listener that runs between start and end, and that GPU stalls (like waiting on getCurrentTexture after a resize) could be contributing to the 200ms frames without showing up as main-thread time. I think the simplest next step is to just add this instrumentation rather than jumping straight to a CDP trace.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":970,"cache_read_input_tokens":139412,"output_tokens":2929,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2434},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":970,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2929,"cache_read_input_tokens":139412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":970,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":970},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":29296,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEmiTUscrDUbd5Z7Srgu","requestRef":"7139d177-26ae-4f64-a452-2c869e6b60b3","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3afb3807-319a-44e4-a974-b220e53b5345","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:44:28.758Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"3afb3807-319a-44e4-a974-b220e53b5345","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEmiTphmnaDcTod48FPP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Idle and wheel scrolling perform identically between modes, but the sidebar toggle regresses badly in liquid mode (44 slow frames vs 4, with spikes to 200ms) due to per-frame canvas resizing. I'll dig into where that time is being spent.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":970,"cache_read_input_tokens":139412,"output_tokens":2929,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2434},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":970,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2929,"cache_read_input_tokens":139412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":970,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":970},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":10,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEmiTUscrDUbd5Z7Srgu","requestRef":"7139d177-26ae-4f64-a452-2c869e6b60b3","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6a6b23bc-0e0d-4404-89fc-c53fbe05c40d","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:44:28.780Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
