{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","id":"8a28cf04-489f-4df4-b7a3-48ce51044d0d","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:47:16.923Z","version":"2.1.305","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"a9ed8921dc21a185c51f032ab201ef86db193f2b4a3c27f0d2631dc37b2aa860","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"xhigh"}},"base":"385e723b-7be9-4f97-bf4d-5d5f0a87892e","keep":170,"tail":["1c1fb6ccc429fcf6e854d997ca1db01ad39653ba3c0c72ede8b3a790c4f1f149","e17238b3ac654a6bc98af2bd4e564ccde81d0369d50118b3ad52f673910a7e27","35469e2f1043702ac7c36711e02e489ecf3a7a24b80d359d084488cc234cb284"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",172,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"8eda64150a8089a7121c3a3f20ff8f5f4ef101816cc2915e052346de6d949518"}
{"parentUuid":"b98dbd1c-4736-4709-9b7d-a022cf1056fd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEmy5BMSMcc5EdGdrDJY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Canvas width is now fixed at 1280, but frames during the slide are still running at roughly half-rate, around 26.7ms each, dropping the effective framerate to about 37fps instead of 75. I'm trying to figure out what's causing this slowdown, possibly something in the copy or render step.\n\nThe likely culprit is copyElementImageToTexture during layout changes — since content resizes every frame, the whole element has to be re-rastered into the texture each time, unlike scroll where content just shifts position and tiles can be reused. The 11.8ms draw times suggest the synchronous raster/copy step is expensive, much higher than scroll's median of 1.4ms, and the 26.7ms frames likely reflect genuine GPU-bound work from re-rastering resized images plus the glass compositing passes each frame.\n\nI'm also weighing how much the sidebar-slide regression actually matters practically — 37fps for 300ms versus 75fps in CSS mode is a real but brief dip, and worth checking whether scroll's per-frame raster is somehow cheaper due to translation-only compositing versus the masonry relayout happening during the slide.\n\nI wonder if the real cause is the ResizeObserver cycle: setting content size triggers syncShapes to read rects, forcing a synchronous layout, which then cascades into virtuoso's own resize callbacks and React re-renders — though that same work should occur in CSS mode too. I should get an actual profile rather than guessing, using long-animation-frame attribution or checking main-thread busy time per frame to see if these slow frames are GPU-bound rather than script-bound.\n\nSince LoAF only flags frames over 50ms, I'd need deeper CDP tracing to see main-thread task durations alongside GPU process activity per frame. As a faster alternative, I could run targeted experiments — disabling the glass render while keeping the copy step to isolate whether rendering or copying is the bottleneck, possibly by monkeypatching GPUQueue methods to no-op and measuring the effect.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1196,"cache_read_input_tokens":154522,"output_tokens":2173,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1496},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1196,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2173,"cache_read_input_tokens":154522,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1196,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1196},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":18193,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEmy4kZK7G16sG669T39","requestRef":"8a28cf04-489f-4df4-b7a3-48ce51044d0d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"22dd8edc-527b-447b-8238-b627a9f35262","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:47:35.837Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
