{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","id":"f65932e0-832e-4798-9f89-5abfa8714f00","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:48:10.537Z","version":"2.1.305","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"a9ed8921dc21a185c51f032ab201ef86db193f2b4a3c27f0d2631dc37b2aa860","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"xhigh"}},"base":"6ac50387-c2c8-4307-a86a-ec2950bd79a6","keep":182,"tail":["57822c940d91b84ade2712f6de8673efabac6f6c2faccc71551b6c01451d028c","63cc22616ceffaefe9ec7a3e2639557c93666eab1d1666475079b58e9bd6c517","5a4a107416cc7a791495ed5a786d07585688990fdd405fa6a84d2dba46c225e9"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",184,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"8f8cfc6bdbbe2677387c9097af554ba6762a90f21f2754d8abdd5ed9b0e18213"}
{"parentUuid":"b94e2765-7618-4533-ab31-b21629b21658","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEn32Ja9qWHb3LFoeijs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm tallying up the per-frame GPU passes at full screen resolution — compositing the HTML backdrop, running the adaptive blur chain across downsampled levels, computing the displacement field, generating the shadow mask with blur and composite, rendering the glass container, and finally blitting to output — plus accounting for the multiple submit calls this likely requires.\n\nThat's roughly 8-12 full-screen passes at 0.92MP, which is bandwidth-heavy for integrated GPUs, especially since most of the canvas output ends up identical to the unchanged backdrop. I'm thinking about a spatial optimization that avoids touching liquid-dom internals: since only the toolbar strip and edge tab region actually need glass effects, I could render the glass core into a smaller output texture sized just to that region, while the rest of the canvas is a direct copy of the content — this means figuring out how to translate the core's transform and whether the Html node supports positioning offsets to make this work.\n\nI'm now working out the actual compositing: copy the full-size content texture directly into the canvas texture as the base layer, then copy the smaller strip-glass result on top at the correct offset using copyTextureToTexture, which acts like a cheap DMA copy as long as formats and sizes line up and the canvas texture is configured with COPY_DST usage.\n\nI'm also checking the alpha handling—since the stage content has an opaque background, opaque alphaMode should be fine, and I need to confirm the html entry texture's device dimensions actually match the canvas's device pixel size exactly.\n\nFor the strip scene, I'm thinking through how to render only a subregion: the core render takes width/height/dpr for its targets, and the Html layer's compositing depends on the scene's transform mapping screen coordinates into the html texture. If I shift the scene root (or container) transform by -stripTop, both the Html layer and glass shapes should move correctly together, assuming the Scene exposes a way to apply a root-level offset.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2489,"cache_read_input_tokens":162727,"output_tokens":1718,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1559},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2489,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1718,"cache_read_input_tokens":162727,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2489,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2489},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":19028,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEn31xjEHPntDGpsM12K","requestRef":"f65932e0-832e-4798-9f89-5abfa8714f00","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c577f7b1-4241-4b76-9ba4-5c2de0ec5910","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:48:30.161Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
