{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","id":"bc29dcc5-2587-482b-9e79-903cf8d8f84b","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:49:10.762Z","version":"2.1.305","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"a9ed8921dc21a185c51f032ab201ef86db193f2b4a3c27f0d2631dc37b2aa860","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"xhigh"}},"base":"aa0166d4-b7d2-4dd3-a5f8-2dce37453154","keep":197,"tail":["90d50dcc0add0effb7295a5a842413e0dbae159f80f2c6244e74093edfcad0d4","8edb5023e28486b9a52ac2a24bae664b019843c6f52007b5cb7960d3ddbd1131","d3e65c65b8091576a8d9cbf8e3d1184260e03ee6867075a39d69298780e0acc8"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",199,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"815f20309f900adf0421694e75532a9eb0311769888a1eb94a4d4add07f765ec"}
{"parentUuid":"6ffae3b3-afc2-4874-99ec-b015b9f60c23","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEn7Tk8TNfiTWwoqmrFe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm checking that the HTML entry texture supports copy operations, accounting for cases where the texture is larger than the device size and the copy region needs to be clamped to the canvas dimensions. I'm also considering how core.render triggers syncTargets to recreate intermediate targets whenever width or height changes, which matters if the strip size shifts frequently during things like a sidebar slide animation.\n\nTo avoid stalls from constant target reallocation, I'm thinking of making the strip a fixed full-canvas-width band covering only the vertical range where shapes appear, quantizing the height to a multiple of 64 device pixels so toolbar movement during the slide doesn't trigger reallocs. Since most shapes (edge tab, toolbar, query chip) sit near the top of the canvas, the strip height stays small relative to the full canvas, though I still need to check whether the library continues painting when hidden behind an overlay.\n\nNow I'm sketching the general draw logic: sync layers, get the backdrop entry, then decide whether the band covers the whole canvas (render directly, no copies) or just a sub-region (allocate a band texture only when its size changes, shift the container vertically to render just that band, then composite the entry texture and band texture into the output via copy commands before submitting). I'm still working out how the container's transform should behave in this compositing step.\n\nFor that layer, the core calls getSceneHtmlEntry, so I need to return an adjusted inverseTransform that accounts for the band offset — composing the layer's inverse transform with a translation by the top offset before inverting, so output device coordinates map correctly back to local CSS coordinates.\n\nI'm also checking whether writeHtmlCompositeParams needs anything else from the entry beyond width/height/opacity, which stay unchanged, and confirming the canvas dimensions used in the shader globals correspond to the band size. For the remaining content source methods like atlasTexture and getGlassContentRange, I'm considering wrapping the source in a Proxy so those delegate through untouched while only the transform gets intercepted.\n\nI need to bind proxied methods to the original target rather than the proxy itself, since private class fields would break otherwise, and I'm treating the type mismatch by just casting the proxy to the expected interface. I'm also confirming that blur and other band-local passes clamp correctly at the top and bottom edges of each band.\n\nI'm reasoning through how much margin to add around shapes to safely contain the shadow and blur falloff — accounting for shadow offset plus blur radius, then converting the padded CSS-pixel band boundaries into device-pixel coordinates using the device pixel ratio.\n\nI want to quantize the band height to avoid frequent texture reallocation when shapes animate (like a query chip sliding in), since resizing render targets every frame would cause stalls. My plan is to make the band \"sticky\" — grow immediately when needed but resist shrinking, quantizing to a fixed device-pixel multiple to keep allocations stable.\n\nI need to verify where the capture-error toast and other UI elements sit, since if something sits far from the top it would permanently inflate the band; checking the CSS shows most elements (toolbar, chip, edge tab) are near the top, which keeps the band bounded.\n\nThen for the final output step, I'm confirming the texture format matches what was passed to the device setup so the copy to the canvas output works correctly.\n\nFor sizing, I use the smaller of the copied content dimensions and the output texture dimensions, since on the first frame before anything's copied the area is just transparent black (WebGPU clears canvas textures to transparent black each frame), which is fine since that area is clipped anyway before the first real content copy happens.\n\nFor the band copy, I position it at the top with width matching the canvas and height clamped so it never exceeds the output bounds. I also need to double check that the html entry texture's actual dimensions aren't padded larger than the device width, since copying from the origin with minimum sizes should still be safe either way.\n\nI'm also reasoning through whether copyTextureToTexture preserves the html layer's opacity and blur settings correctly — with opacity 1 and blur 0, it should match the composited result exactly, since the core path renders html over a cleared black scene and transparent pixels end up black in both cases under opaque alpha mode. I'm also considering premultiplied alpha behavior, but for fully opaque content both paths should produce identical results regardless.\n\nThinking through the render cost breakdown: the band passes stay small while the full-size cost is just the element copy plus one cheap full-size texture copy. I'm checking whether WebGpuDomContentSource.sync() does any extra GPU work like blur filtering, but it shouldn't need to here since there's no blur to apply. Now I'm sketching out the LiquidSurface class, adding band tracking state and a bandTexture field, then working out how setShapes computes the band region from the shapes.\n\nI'm pulling the band computation into a pure, testable function in liquidGlassShape.ts that takes shapes, device pixel ratio, and canvas height, then derives the top and height of the glass band by expanding the shape bounds with a margin to account for shadow and refraction reach, snapping to a device-pixel step.\n\nI'm reasoning through edge cases: if the top edge shifts because shapes slide vertically, only the container offset changes (cheap), while the texture only needs reallocation when the quantized height actually changes.\n\nI also realize band recomputation needs to happen on resize too, since dpr or canvas height changes should trigger it — simplest fix is computing the band directly inside draw() from current glass values rather than relying on the per-glass change detection in setShapes.\n\nIn draw(), I'm handling the case where the glass band covers the full canvas by rendering straight into the output texture, and otherwise only passing the affected rows through liquid-dom's full pipeline.\n\nI'm thinking through where sync() needs to be called — since it's what triggers the content copy, it should run once per paint right after setting container.y, before building the content layers for the encoder.\n\nChecking that core.render submits its own command buffers before my encoder submits the content and band copies, so ordering stays correct: content copy then band copy into output, both after the core renders into bandTexture. If the band has zero height I can skip the core render step entirely and just copy content. I also need to handle resizing the band texture when dimensions change, destroying and recreating it as needed.\n\nFor the actual copies, I'm clamping the band copy region to not exceed the canvas height, and clamping the content copy to the minimum of the copied device dimensions and the target width/height, skipping entirely if the size is zero or the texture is missing.\n\nNow I'm working out how the bandSource proxy shifts the inverse transform for the offset top position, storing the current band top so the getter can adjust the matrix's translation terms per draw, and checking whether the scene HTML entry type is properly exported from the core package for spreading.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1513,"cache_read_input_tokens":174757,"output_tokens":6059,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5727},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1513,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6059,"cache_read_input_tokens":174757,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1513,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1513},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":58376,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEn7TSmvsKwE9pygjXKo","requestRef":"bc29dcc5-2587-482b-9e79-903cf8d8f84b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f73d009a-d48e-48fb-b90c-cd68c712d0bd","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:50:09.825Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"f73d009a-d48e-48fb-b90c-cd68c712d0bd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEn7Tk8TNfiTWwoqmrFe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Html textures carry `COPY_SRC`, and the backdrop's sampling is a plain 2D matrix I can shift. Checking the public types before writing it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1513,"cache_read_input_tokens":174757,"output_tokens":6059,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5727},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1513,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6059,"cache_read_input_tokens":174757,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1513,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1513},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEn7TSmvsKwE9pygjXKo","requestRef":"bc29dcc5-2587-482b-9e79-903cf8d8f84b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8bc71bf8-1a09-4721-ac4d-fe8cbed5aecc","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:50:09.840Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
