{"parentUuid":"26c7ded8-673d-4718-9c9c-5eb9bdef120c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01UbtyiK9fy5Ms1M2MrDbwqN","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1be8b44e-1248-40bd-9253-7b618ee920d0","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:50:42.830Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"1be8b44e-1248-40bd-9253-7b618ee920d0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEnC49hn9dBKCqF3dmxe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Since WebGpuGlassContentSource is just a plain object type, I realize I can construct my own object that proxies the properties from the DOM content source, since it implements the interface and exposes the needed members like atlasTexture.\n\nNext I want to write the glassBand pure function, which computes which device-pixel rows of the canvas contain glass shapes in CSS pixels, accounting for margin and texture reallocation steps. I'm also checking that capture-error and query-chip elements stay near the top of the capture bar.\n\nWriting band calculation function...\n\nI'm tracing through a few examples to verify the band-clamping logic: no shapes returns zero, a toolbar pill rounds up to a 256px band, a lens shape clamps to the canvas height, and a shape positioned far down the canvas produces the correct offset band within bounds.\n\nNow I'm shifting to the LiquidSurface changes — configuring context usage for render attachment and copy destination, and setting the container's y-offset based on the band before sync() runs, since the layers' transform depends on that being set beforehand. I'm also double-checking that updating container.y won't incorrectly trigger a full DOM content recopy during sync.\n\nWriting draw function...\n\nStill writing texture copy logic...\n\nThe area outside content within the html host should stay transparent against the opaque canvas, properly clipped by the wrapper. For the band rendering, I'm checking that the shader correctly maps fragment coordinates back through the shift to sample html local coordinates. I'm also verifying packShapes handles the container transform (translation and dpr scaling) correctly, and whether the core needs any Y-flip relative to height for glass shapes.\n\nBackdrop metrics for adaptive specular only matter if that readback feature is enabled, so I can skip it here. I'm defining a bandTarget helper that recreates the band texture when dimensions change, plus a destroy method to clean up the texture. The output texture just needs RENDER_ATTACHMENT usage since the core renders into it directly, and resize() correctly triggers a repaint.\n\nsetShapes also triggers requestPaint since the band gets recomputed during draw, and I'll keep the existing first-frame callback logic that checks for a copied device width before firing onFirstFrame. Now I'll write the actual code.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":985,"cache_read_input_tokens":183075,"output_tokens":4024,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2903},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":985,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4024,"cache_read_input_tokens":183075,"cache_creation_input_tokens":985,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":985},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":28858,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEnC3s5ZzMDotQKhnhxF","requestRef":"c8f9d553-744b-416b-b1c2-59e5fb31ef8a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"25ecfd84-0484-47cb-bdce-c2ce042cbdc0","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:50:42.827Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slu