{"parentUuid":"0f6f0bdd-0d6a-458b-934f-c93e8581c50d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEnW7ytUbZxkzQs9emeg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"With banding, the element copy cost dominates now—full re-raster is 12/7, copy-off drops to 1/0, submit-off is 4/3. That copy cost comes from Chromium rasterizing changed elements into the texture, which is inherent to HTML-in-Canvas; during the sidebar slide the whole layout shifts, forcing a full re-raster each frame. I'm thinking about ways to cut that copy cost down.\n\nOne lead: the copy targets the full backdrop host (100vw x 100vh canvas), not just the smaller stage, though raster cost should scale with painted content rather than empty space. More importantly, I recall the earlier note that large images caused big hitches while small thumbnails didn't—so I want to check whether the library cards in this preview are using full-size seed images instead of proper thumbnails, since rasterizing oversized images every frame could be the real culprit. I should check the natural width of the card images to confirm.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1167,"cache_read_input_tokens":200344,"output_tokens":804,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":542},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1167,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":804,"cache_read_input_tokens":200344,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1167,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1167},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":9095,"thinkingDisplay"