{"parentUuid":"f0af2e1b-1ac2-437d-aa83-c769deaf8a13","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14525804 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"05b47a14-54ba-4927-8743-89520c8ec457","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:54:49.483Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14525804 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"709e39b0af3c6aaaaa702076de7ae6ace29acb02042fbeeb7725f2e59576e6a2","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The preview seed cards are using full-size images rather than thumbnails, which matches the expensive-rendering issue flagged earlier. I want to check how large the desktop app's generated thumbnails actually are, since if they're much smaller than the raw images, the real app's per-frame cost should be far lower than what the preview is simulating.\n\nI'm thinking through how to validate this without a full build: I could try swapping the seed images for downscaled versions directly in the running preview via CDP, drawing them into a canvas and replacing the image src with the smaller blob, then rerunning the slide test. The tricky part is whether virtuoso's re-renders would reset those swapped attributes during scrolling.\n\nRather than fight that, I consider intercepting the network layer with CDP's Fetch domain to serve downscaled JPEGs for the seed-demo image URLs, generating them on the fly via canvas resizing — elaborate but workable. Still, I wonder if it's even necessary, since the earlier note already confirmed 560px thumbnails caused zero hitches, meaning the heavy seed images are really just a preview-only artifact rather than a real issue.\n\nBut I realize the real app also pulls in remote images like og:image previews and YouTube posters at much larger native sizes, which aren't pre-thumbnailed locally, so downsampling those per-frame could matter more. To get a credible number, I think it's worth running the Fetch-interception experiment: enabling CDP's Fetch domain and, in-page, resizing fetched images via createImageBitmap and OffscreenCanvas before returning them.\n\nI'll scope the Fetch interception to only image resource types matching the seed-demo pattern, since a page-level fetch() call wouldn't be caught by that filter anyway. The plan is to pre-generate base64 thumbnails for all the seed-demo jpgs before reload, then enable Fetch interception, reload, and fulfill requests with those thumbnails, then measure both modes — it's a bit of extra scripting work, but the resulting comparison would be worth it.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The preview seed is loading full-size 6000×4000 photos into 332px cards — exactly what the Paper note warned about, since the real app uses generated thumbnails instead. I'll check the thumbnail size so I can test with realistic images.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XT5PkPZ4CEVfjBBcYQ6Ugp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && grep -rn \"createThumbnail\\b\\|createThumbnail =\" electron/*.mjs | head -5; grep -rn \"resize(\\|maxDimension\\|THUMBNAIL_\\|thumbnailSize\" electron/*.mjs | head -10","description":"Find desktop thumbnail dimensions"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
