{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","prNumber":170,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Squidys-Tools/inkling/pull/170","prRepository":"Squidys-Tools/inkling","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:56:34.556Z"}
{"parentUuid":"98b7df0f-e0a8-4bb2-b9eb-325cd06f95f1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEngB5h8doW7B13Pf4Ve","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"With thumbnail-size images, scrolling shows parity between liquid and CSS modes, but the sidebar toggle reveals liquid mode dropping roughly every other frame during the ~300ms slide animation, compared to CSS's near-perfect performance — though each miss is just a single vsync, nothing severe.\n\nThe remaining regression comes from re-copying the whole element into a texture every frame during relayout, since liquid mode lacks tile caching like Chromium's native rasterizer. One possible fix is throttling the texture copy to every other frame during the slide, letting content lag by one frame — though I need to think through how that stale-pixel lag would look against the sidebar's live DOM edge, since the canvas moves with the stage but its contents would be rendered for a previous width.\n\nAnother idea: freeze the library content width during the slide and only translate it, reflowing once the animation settles — cheaper for both modes but changes the tuned look of the transition, so that feels out of scope for now. I think the remaining cost — occasional dropped frames during a 300ms transition, with scroll and idle performance at parity — is an acceptable, honestly-reportable mild regression, though I should flag the untested case of 144Hz displays where per-frame budgets are tighter.\n\nChecking whether the whole host element gets copied even for partial changes, I note scroll already touches the whole content anyway, so this isn't a real inefficiency. Remaining things to verify: pinned search query chips becoming liquid when a query is pinned via Enter, grid/list view toggle transitions, hover-triggered paint events on cards, and the card-opening flight animation into the overlay.\n\nFor the flight animation, I want to grab a mid-flight screenshot since it may use a cloned element whose rect validity inside a canvas context is unclear. I should also check whether cards are draggable, since Chromium's drag-image generation for elements inside a layout subtree canvas might render blank — worth grepping for `draggable` in the component. Focus rings already look fine from an earlier screenshot showing the orange outline rendering correctly inside the canvas.\n\nAccessibility should be fine since canvas children with layoutsubtree remain hit-testable and accessible per spec. I'm now wondering about other views like archive and serendipity nested in the library scroll, specifically whether backdrop-filter effects (like on the archive delete button or video badge) actually render properly when copied into a canvas subtree — I don't see a video card in screenshot 03, so I want to track one down to verify.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":733,"cache_read_input_tokens":209223,"output_tokens":2189,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1927},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":733,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2189,"cache_read_input_tokens":209223,"cache_creation_input_tokens":733,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":733},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":24275,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEngAhPE6cPXDDH1eVeG","requestRef":"48e9a8c0-90b5-48aa-9c0f-67ecb07cbd79","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"89402178-2ab4-4ac5-a1f0-0661336b80c3","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:56:59.661Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"89402178-2ab4-4ac5-a1f0-0661336b80c3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEngB5h8doW7B13Pf4Ve","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wheel scrolling now performs on par between liquid and CSS modes, and idle shows no paints either way; the sidebar slide remains the only gap, with liquid dropping occasional single frames (max 27ms) due to Chromium re-rasterizing the reflowing grid each frame, while CSS stays near zero. Now checking the in-grid surfaces that still use CSS glass (video badge) and the pinned query chip.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":733,"cache_read_input_tokens":209223,"output_tokens":2189,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1927},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":733,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2189,"cache_read_input_tokens":209223,"cache_creation_input_tokens":733,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":733},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":18,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEngAhPE6cPXDDH1eVeG","requestRef":"48e9a8c0-90b5-48aa-9c0f-67ecb07cbd79","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0a8b6022-24b7-4a1c-9080-3b4ed84f7e7c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:56:59.695Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-s