{"parentUuid":"4c61bcea-88e8-4c13-8194-9fc9d81c1e57","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01FswhEwnmYC11JknKf1zjzk","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0f18b14a-485b-4e7c-8334-ba60bf467abf","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:58:34.164Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"0f18b14a-485b-4e7c-8334-ba60bf467abf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEnnfrjtACNdxoxPpfXR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The archive-card-delete button sits inside the library canvas's backdrop content, so if the canvas drew liquid glass over it, the button's own icon would get refracted and tinted along with everything else — unless it's rendered outside the canvas entirely. Better to just keep it as CSS.\n\nOther candidates like note-editor-actions are nearly opaque already, so they don't really count as translucent. Reader-view buttons (close, font picker) sit over content that can't easily move into a canvas — remote images without CORS, embedded iframes, text selection concerns — so those stay CSS too. At this point I've converted every `.glass` button except card-video-badge, which is just decorative, so the core translucent button system is now fully migrated.\n\nFor the reader specifically, putting its content into a canvas would blank out remote images (no CORS attr, headers blocked) and break iframe embeds like YouTube since cross-origin iframes don't paint into canvas — that's unacceptable, so reader close/font-picker stay CSS, same with archive-card-delete since it's in-grid.\n\nNow I'm thinking about documentation — AGENTS.md wants doc checks, and since this change spans main process (CORS headers) and renderer (canvas rendering), it's worth a short note in docs/tech-stack.md about the liquid-glass approach and CSS fallback strategy.\n\nI also need to check the changelog since there's an \"Added: liquid glass on toolbar controls and zoom pill\" entry under Unreleased that should be kept current, then make sure Biome, typecheck, and tests all pass on the changed files, and clean up Electron plus registry restoration. As for committing — AGENTS says only commit or push when the user explicitly asks, and I'm not sure the user actually asked for that in this conversation versus it being inferred from the task summary, so I should hold off on committing without confirming first.\n\nI'll leave the branch uncommitted and offer at the end to commit and push to PR #170 rather than assuming. Before wrapping up, I still want to verify the LiquidGlass crossOrigin handling behaves correctly across the Electron and web preview builds, since the web preview falls back to CSS without `layoutSubtree`.\n\nI'm also double-checking the `onHeadersReceived` logic in main.mjs for how it handles existing CORS headers, and confirming Electron's resourceType naming matches \"image\" for the relevant case.\n\nYes, the CORS-mode image request would send an `Origin: app://local` header to remote servers, which could theoretically trip up rare hotlink-protection setups checking Origin, though Referer behavior stays essentially unchanged — so this is a minor, low-risk consideration rather than a real blocker.\n\nChecking other image sources in the library grid: video posters and avatars are already covered, favicon-style images only appear in the grep'd sites, and there are no remote background-image CSS usages to worry about. X post cards don't use iframes, onboarding isn't part of the library canvas, and I'm now considering whether the Serendipity empty-state view has any continuous animations worth a closer QA look.\n\nThinking about Serendipity's infinite CSS animations and the processing spinner on disabled cards — in liquid mode, a spinner's infinite animation would trigger a full-canvas element copy and band render on every frame, meaning continuous GPU raster of the entire content during background jobs like OCR or embeddings, unlike CSS mode where only the spinner's tiny region repaints. This continuous-repaint cost during idle processing states is exactly the concern worth flagging.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1031,"cache_read_input_tokens":219294,"output_tokens":2747,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2620},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1031,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2747,"cache_read_input_tokens":219294,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1031,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1031},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":30814,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEnnfVugXnQtmAmCSbST","requestRef":"7a5e21c9-a491-4454-b0b8-5992287838d6","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"11dd0e04-c29b-4a12-8d50-5bad7778c1db","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:58:34.163Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"11dd0e04-c29b-4a12-8d50-5bad7778c1db","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEnnfrjtACNdxoxPpfXR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All `.glass` buttons are now liquid except the video badge and reader controls, which can't use canvas due to iframe/backdrop-filter limitations. Next, I'll check for looping animations in the grid, since those would force a costly full-canvas copy every frame.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1031,"cache_read_input_tokens":219294,"output_tokens":2747,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2620},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1031,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2747,"cache_read_input_tokens":219294,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1031,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1031},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":9,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEnnfVugXnQtmAmCSbST","requestRef":"7a5e21c9-a491-4454-b0b8-5992287838d6","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ff79c5cd-09fd-46e8-b53e-471261f6d523","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:58:34.189Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
