{"parentUuid":"ae2526ec-fd8a-4f62-b2d0-6f2bcc6abc1a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01Tq1L1H3eZ472noUUE3gaiW","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7df9cce6-bd3d-436c-aa4f-d65d5b8eefaf","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:59:50.984Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"7df9cce6-bd3d-436c-aa4f-d65d5b8eefaf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEnurUeq14LmYREGEiBW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm drafting changelog entries: one about the liquid glass refraction effect added to desktop UI elements via WebGPU with a CSS fallback, and another about CORS headers now being added to remote image responses so library cards can request them properly.\n\nI'm also considering whether to add a short note in the security section explaining that the main process exposes a permissive CORS header on image responses specifically so the liquid glass canvas can draw remote card images, since a maintainer reading the security docs might not otherwise realize this cross-boundary behavior exists. I think a single concise sentence there is justified, while a dedicated tech-stack table row for liquid glass isn't necessary since it's already covered in code comments.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2873,"cache_read_input_tokens":235426,"output_tokens":1574,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":703},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2873,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1574,"cache_read_input_tokens":235426,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2873,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2873},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":10019,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEnur1rxkhzzXHyU9RwM","requestRef":"0cb6cbc3-f67c-45cc-85fb-184dd56b52ee","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"db404441-97ad-4917-831e-ab52deba3147","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:59:50.980Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"db404441-97ad-4917-831e-ab52deba3147","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEnurUeq14LmYREGEiBW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll add a changelog entry under Added and one under Changed, plus a note in tech-stack.md's security section about the main process now rewriting a response header, since that's a cross-boundary security change maintainers should be able to find.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2873,"cache_read_input_tokens":235426,"output_tokens":1574,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":703},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2873,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1574,"cache_read_input_tokens":235426,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2873,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2873},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":14,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEnur1rxkhzzXHyU9RwM","requestRef":"0cb6cbc3-f67c-45cc-85fb-184dd56b52ee","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2484f2c4-a817-41cc-b025-f3bc91875ce3","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:59:51.003Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"2484f2c4-a817-41cc-b025-f3bc91875ce3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEnurUeq14LmYREGEiBW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MtYqF96ahuJqdcFogDGHWR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python - <<'EOF'\np='docs/changelog.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nold='''- The item count above the library rolls up when it first appears and replays when hovered, using the React Bits CountUp in compact format (`src/components/CountUp.tsx`, `src/components/AnimatedCount.tsx`)\n'''\nnew='''- The item count above the library rolls up when it first appears and replays when hovered, using the React Bits CountUp in compact format (`src/components/CountUp.tsx`, `src/components/AnimatedCount.tsx`)\n- Liquid glass in the desktop app: the library toolbar, search chip, collapsed sidebar tab and image zoom control refract what is behind them through WebGPU and Chromium's HTML-in-Canvas, and fall back to the CSS glass when either is unavailable (#170)\n'''\nassert s.count(old)==1\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nold2='''- Library list IPC sends card fields only; reader content is loaded from SQLite when opened.\n'''\nnew2='''- Library list IPC sends card fields only; reader content is loaded from SQLite when opened.\n- Library cards load remote images in CORS mode and the desktop app adds a CORS header to image responses, so the liquid glass canvas can draw them; no extra requests are made (#170)\n'''\nassert s.count(old2)==1\ns=s.replace(old2,new2)\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8',newline='').write(s)\np='docs/tech-stack.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nold='''and do not expose arbitrary filesystem or shell commands through the preload bridge.\n'''\nnew='''and do not expose arbitrary filesystem or shell commands through the preload bridge.\n\nThe app session adds `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` to remote image responses so library cards, loaded with `crossorigin`, can be drawn into the liquid glass canvas. That lets the renderer read pixels of images it already displays and nothing more; it changes no request and applies to no other resource type.\n'''\nassert s.count(old)==1\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8',newline='').write(s)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat docs","description":"Add changelog entries and security note"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2873,"cache_read_input_tokens":235426,"output_tokens":1574,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":703},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2873,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1574,"cache_read_input_tokens":235426,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2873,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2873},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MtYqF96ahuJqdcFogDGHWR":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && python - <<'EOF'\np='docs/changelog.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nold='''- The item count above the library rolls up when it first appears and replays when hovered, using the React Bits CountUp in compact format (`src/components/CountUp.tsx`, `src/components/AnimatedCount.tsx`)\n'''\nnew='''- The item count above the library rolls up when it first appears and replays when hovered, using the React Bits CountUp in compact format (`src/components/CountUp.tsx`, `src/components/AnimatedCount.tsx`)\n- Liquid glass in the desktop app: the library toolbar, search chip, collapsed sidebar tab and image zoom control refract what is behind them through WebGPU and Chromium's HTML-in-Canvas, and fall back to the CSS glass when either is unavailable (#170)\n'''\nassert s.count(old)==1\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nold2='''- Library list IPC sends card fields only; reader content is loaded from SQLite when opened.\n'''\nnew2='''- Library list IPC sends card fields only; reader content is loaded from SQLite when opened.\n- Library cards load remote images in CORS mode and the desktop app adds a CORS header to image responses, so the liquid glass canvas can draw them; no extra requests are made (#170)\n'''\nassert s.count(old2)==1\ns=s.replace(old2,new2)\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8',newline='').write(s)\np='docs/tech-stack.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nold='''and do not expose arbitrary filesystem or shell commands through the preload bridge.\n'''\nnew='''and do not expose arbitrary filesystem or shell commands through the preload bridge.\n\nThe app session adds `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` to remote image responses so library cards, loaded with `crossorigin`, can be drawn into the liquid glass canvas. That lets the renderer read pixels of images it already displays and nothing more; it changes no request and applies to no other resource type.\n'''\nassert s.count(old)==1\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8',newline='').write(s)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat docs","description":"Add changelog entries and security note"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01MtYqF96ahuJqdcFogDGHWR":{"cwd":"/c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgEnur1rxkhzzXHyU9RwM","requestRef":"0cb6cbc3-f67c-45cc-85fb-184dd56b52ee","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"bb01469c-4925-4359-8247-210c8fa886bb","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:59:54.041Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"bb01469c-4925-4359-8247-210c8fa886bb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a5d551ad-5e9e-431c-a603-b554797c9ccd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MtYqF96ahuJqdcFogDGHWR","type":"tool_result","content":"warning: in the working copy of 'docs/changelog.md', LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it\nwarning: in the working copy of 'docs/tech-stack.md', LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it\n docs/changelog.md  | 2 ++\n docs/tech-stack.md | 2 ++\n 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5cb72ebb-3d58-412b-baa0-2f370683743c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T04:59:55.203Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"warning: in the working copy of 'docs/changelog.md', LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it\nwarning: in the working copy of 'docs/tech-stack.md', LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it\n docs/changelog.md  | 2 ++\n docs/tech-stack.md | 2 ++\n 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304\\docs\\changelog.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":67,"oldLines":6,"newStart":67,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - Regular Spaces: manual collections alongside saved searches. The Space create form chooses Smart or Regular, a Regular Space holds only the items you file into it from the expanded item view, and the chips there show current membership and take an item back out. Deleting a Space still leaves its items alone (SQU-4, `src-tauri/src/storage.rs`, `src/App.tsx`, `src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx`)"," - Top of Mind: items can be pinned and unpinned from their details view, and the Top of mind view collects them. That view explains itself when nothing is pinned yet, and the main library stays a plain list of everything (SQU-9) (`src/App.tsx`, `src/components/ExpandedItemOverlay.tsx`)"," - The item count above the library rolls up when it first appears and replays when hovered, using the React Bits CountUp in compact format (`src/components/CountUp.tsx`, `src/components/AnimatedCount.tsx`)","+- Liquid glass in the desktop app: the library toolbar, search chip, collapsed sidebar tab and image zoom control refract what is behind them through WebGPU and Chromium's HTML-in-Canvas, and fall back to the CSS glass when either is unavailable (#170)"," "," ### Fixed"," "]},{"oldStart":78,"oldLines":6,"newStart":79,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ### Changed"," "," - Library list IPC sends card fields only; reader content is loaded from SQLite when opened.","+- Library cards load remote images in CORS mode and the desktop app adds a CORS header to image responses, so the liquid glass canvas can draw them; no extra requests are made (#170)"," - Electron defers canvas system-font loading until PDF work runs; BMP and ICO thumbnails use canvas without loading system fonts."," - Library cards form a denser masonry grid with tighter gutters and natural media proportions; note and quote previews stay readable, while list, Archive, and Serendipity views keep their existing geometry."," - Desktop window opens at 960 × 540 instead of 1000 × 800; the 320 × 360 minimum size is unchanged."]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304\\docs\\tech-stack.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":105,"oldLines":6,"newStart":105,"newLines":8,"lines":[" "," Treat all fetched HTML as untrusted. Sanitize article HTML before rendering, allowlist iframe providers, strip scripts/event handlers/unsafe URLs/untrusted `srcdoc`, keep remote content isolated from Electron's privileged main process, and do not expose arbitrary filesystem or shell commands through the preload bridge."," ","+The app session adds `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` to remote image responses so library cards, loaded with `crossorigin`, can be drawn into the liquid glass canvas. That lets the renderer read pixels of images it already displays and nothing more; it changes no request and applies to no other resource type.","+"," ## Update checks"," "," The packaged Windows app checks GitHub Releases once when it opens; it does not poll on a schedule. GitHub receives the request from the device and the app name and installed version in its HTTP user agent, but no library data. An available update appears quietly in the sidebar and is downloaded and installed only after the user selects it; that action checks once more before downloading. Electron updater hashes protect update downloads over HTTPS but do not establish publisher trust. The NSIS installer is not Authenticode-signed, so Windows SmartScreen may warn users when they install it."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304\\docs\\changelog.md","C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304\\docs\\tech-stack.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bb01469c-4925-4359-8247-210c8fa886bb","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
