{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"ecd71c9ee7f5480c563528bc47b1c3a1a6e47203a0e1a1d472e7f633834ea06a","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm drafting changelog entries: one about the liquid glass refraction effect added to desktop UI elements via WebGPU with a CSS fallback, and another about CORS headers now being added to remote image responses so library cards can request them properly.\n\nI'm also considering whether to add a short note in the security section explaining that the main process exposes a permissive CORS header on image responses specifically so the liquid glass canvas can draw remote card images, since a maintainer reading the security docs might not otherwise realize this cross-boundary behavior exists. I think a single concise sentence there is justified, while a dedicated tech-stack table row for liquid glass isn't necessary since it's already covered in code comments.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll add a changelog entry under Added and one under Changed, plus a note in tech-stack.md's security section about the main process now rewriting a response header, since that's a cross-boundary security change maintainers should be able to find.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MtYqF96ahuJqdcFogDGHWR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/chris/.t3/worktrees/inkling/t3-47ff5304 && python - <<'EOF'\np='docs/changelog.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nold='''- The item count above the library rolls up when it first appears and replays when hovered, using the React Bits CountUp in compact format (`src/components/CountUp.tsx`, `src/components/AnimatedCount.tsx`)\n'''\nnew='''- The item count above the library rolls up when it first appears and replays when hovered, using the React Bits CountUp in compact format (`src/components/CountUp.tsx`, `src/components/AnimatedCount.tsx`)\n- Liquid glass in the desktop app: the library toolbar, search chip, collapsed sidebar tab and image zoom control refract what is behind them through WebGPU and Chromium's HTML-in-Canvas, and fall back to the CSS glass when either is unavailable (#170)\n'''\nassert s.count(old)==1\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nold2='''- Library list IPC sends card fields only; reader content is loaded from SQLite when opened.\n'''\nnew2='''- Library list IPC sends card fields only; reader content is loaded from SQLite when opened.\n- Library cards load remote images in CORS mode and the desktop app adds a CORS header to image responses, so the liquid glass canvas can draw them; no extra requests are made (#170)\n'''\nassert s.count(old2)==1\ns=s.replace(old2,new2)\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8',newline='').write(s)\np='docs/tech-stack.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nold='''and do not expose arbitrary filesystem or shell commands through the preload bridge.\n'''\nnew='''and do not expose arbitrary filesystem or shell commands through the preload bridge.\n\nThe app session adds `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` to remote image responses so library cards, loaded with `crossorigin`, can be drawn into the liquid glass canvas. That lets the renderer read pixels of images it already displays and nothing more; it changes no request and applies to no other resource type.\n'''\nassert s.count(old)==1\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8',newline='').write(s)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat docs","description":"Add changelog entries and security note"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
