{"parentUuid":"6ba25309-ab96-4219-9feb-9523b239fefe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEnysJcWPLD7YNa4YD2j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm putting together the final report for the user—keeping it concise with screenshots, a small performance table, what wasn't converted and why, and flagging untested areas like 144Hz displays, weak GPUs, and the fully packaged app build, since I only tested in Electron preview mode rather than the real packaged binary. I should also flag the CORS header decision for sign-off, since that was only verified in the preview environment's main process.\n\nI need to clearly flag the CORS header change since it's a security posture shift I made without explicit approval, even though it's not a new network call—the user should get a chance to veto it. I'll also ask whether to commit and push to #170, briefly remind them of the earlier open questions around Settings defaults, empty smart Space links, and the #174 merge, pick 3-4 representative screenshots, and lay out the performance numbers comparing idle, scroll, sidebar toggle, and zoom pan behavior before writing the summary in plain, outcome-first language.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":648,"cache_read_input_tokens":248387,"output_tokens":1737,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":572},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":648,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1737,"cache_read_input_tokens":248387,"cache_creation_input_tokens":648,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":648},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":13008,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEnyrx31HbZkrv3H3Xsi","requestRef":"91c51fb5-f85a-4d4e-8309-f90771b4a4d9","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"606c934c-d181-4bb2-8b94-e6ef171657e0","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:00:48.266Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"606c934c-d181-4bb2-8b94-e6ef171657e0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEnysJcWPLD7YNa4YD2j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Liquid glass is now the default on every translucent button in the library. It's working in the desktop shell, with CSS glass as the fallback. The one leftover cost is that the sidebar slide drops a few single frames. I tested in the Electron preview, not a packaged `build:dir` app, and nothing is committed yet.\n\n![Toolbar glass over scrolled cards](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\liquid-glass\\10-scrolled-under.png)\n![Toolbar close-up](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\liquid-glass\\11-toolbar-closeup.png)\n![Zoom pill lens](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\liquid-glass\\12-lens-closeup.png)\n\n**What's liquid now:**\n- **Toolbar:** back/forward, grid/list, search, the pinned search chip and the capture error.\n- **Collapsed sidebar tab.**\n- **Zoom pill in the image view.** It gets its own pill-sized canvas showing a copy of the thumbnail behind it, so panning stays cheap and the full-size original never goes under glass.\n\n**Left as CSS glass, on purpose:**\n- **Video badge on cards:** it sits inside the grid that the glass refracts, so it can't sit on top of it.\n- **Reader's Close button and font picker:** the reader can't render through a canvas. Embedded videos are cross-site iframes, which the canvas doesn't draw.\n\n**Performance**, same build, liquid vs CSS. I used 512px images to match the real app's thumbnails, because the preview's sample photos are full-size (up to 6000px):\n\n| | Liquid | CSS |\n|---|---|---|\n| Idle (redraws in 2s) | 0 | 0 |\n| Wheel scroll (frames over 25ms) | 0–1 | 1–4 |\n| Sidebar slide (frames over 25ms) | 18–34, max 27ms | 0–4 |\n| Panning the zoomed image | 0 | — |\n\nThe sidebar slide started with spikes of 200–330ms. Three changes brought it down:\n- **Canvas sized to the window**, not the library area. Resizing the canvas was stalling the GPU on every frame of the slide.\n- **Glass drawn only in the toolbar strip.** The glass library re-renders the whole canvas many times per frame, so now it only draws the band of rows that hold glass. The rest of the frame is a plain copy.\n- **Glass shapes update in the same frame**, instead of trailing the buttons by one.\n\nThe remaining cost is Chromium re-drawing the reflowing grid into the canvas on each frame of the slide. That's built into this approach.\n\n**Needs your sign-off.** Remote card images (article previews, video posters) came out blank in the canvas, because Chromium won't draw images from other sites into it unless they're loaded in CORS mode. Cards now load them that way, and the app adds the CORS header to image responses (`electron/main.mjs`). No new requests are made, and it only lets the app read pixels of images it already shows. I noted it in `docs/tech-stack.md` and the changelog. Say if you'd rather handle it another way.\n\n**Not tested:** weak GPUs, 144Hz displays, and the packaged app with a real library.\n\nShould I commit and push this to #170? Your two earlier questions and the offer to bring the recent commits into #174 are still open too."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":648,"cache_read_input_tokens":248387,"output_tokens":1737,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":572},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":648,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1737,"cache_read_input_tokens":248387,"cache_creation_input_tokens":648,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":648},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgEnyrx31HbZkrv3H3Xsi","requestRef":"91c51fb5-f85a-4d4e-8309-f90771b4a4d9","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"21d1c181-e521-4107-8b88-4b39b4aff214","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:00:51.696Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.305","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
