{"parentUuid":"d30897f1-b13e-4ba0-b319-7a7b681c8fec","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFMoTyitojMGiFwFZU5e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm realizing the current animation shrinks the sidebar width while content stays left-anchored, which visually reads as the sidebar being pushed left rather than collapsing in place. What the user actually wants is for the sidebar to remain fixed and not shift position at all.\n\nA better approach: make the sidebar absolutely positioned at full width behind the main content, and instead animate the main content's left margin so it slides over the stationary sidebar. This keeps the same reflow cost as before but gets the visual behavior right, so I need to check the z-index stacking, the main-content CSS, and how the open/closed state classes are applied in the TSX to wire this up correctly.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4499,"cache_read_input_tokens":52407,"output_tokens":924,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":612},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4499,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":924,"cache_read_input_tokens":52407,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4499,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4499},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":9398,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFMoTePPJYfhd86PMCFZ","requestRef":"1ba7eb86-995d-4669-9b81-66de17e6e2ba","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b3e408d0-90fc-4f5b-9283-d05572156bf4","ti