{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","prNumber":174,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Squidys-Tools/inkling/pull/174","prRepository":"Squidys-Tools/inkling","timestamp":"2026-10-21T12:11:14.057Z"}
{"parentUuid":"43a365f8-c4c8-4077-b281-ad7bea635f02","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFMpeF9mqYb17Rey61BD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"For desktop sizes, I'm positioning the sidebar absolutely with a fixed width, avoiding width or opacity transitions, and instead using a delayed visibility change so it becomes unfocusable only after it's fully hidden under the main content.\n\nMain content gets an opaque library-frame background with rounded corners that visually overlap the sidebar, creating the card-sliding-over effect, but I need to think through z-index layering carefully — if main gets a z-index to sit above the sidebar, that could trap or displace other fixed elements like the mascot or modals that currently rely on the default stacking order, so I need to check where those are rendered before assigning z-index values.\n\nInstead, a safer approach might be lowering the sidebar's z-index to auto rather than raising main's, since both are flex items and DOM order alone would put main (which comes after sidebar) on top. I still need to verify whether anything inside the sidebar, like context menus or popovers, needs to extend above main content.\n\nSince sidebar overflow is hidden, that clips any overflowing menus anyway, so stacking order there is less of a concern. For the layout itself, I need to figure out how main-content's margin-left responds to the sidebar's open/closed state, likely using a sibling selector pattern depending on the DOM structure between those two elements.\n\nI also need to check where the edge-tab is rendered and whether its left position syncs with the sidebar width transition, and whether it lives inside main-content or the app-shell wrapper.\n\nOn performance, the margin-left animation still causes the same per-frame reflow of main-content as the old width-based approach did, which was the original concern. I'm weighing whether translating main-content instead would avoid that, but it'd clip content when opening, so sticking with margin seems like the safer tradeoff.\n\nWhen the sidebar is closed and hidden beneath main, the visible sliver under the rounded corner showing sidebar content is actually the intended effect, and the border stays transparent on desktop with opacity at 1. I should also add a delayed visibility-hidden for focus handling, so let me check the DOM structure to confirm.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2878,"cache_read_input_tokens":58468,"output_tokens":2045,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1742},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2878,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2045,"cache_read_input_tokens":58468,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2878},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":21729,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFMpdtZc3MDvQSm96SF9","requestRef":"669fa837-af06-475c-912f-c865e296622f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1b45c02f-32af-4860-978a-f76f6ef39c3a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T12:11:39.361Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
