{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"a9b5274c7e6089b81bdfee1edadf84087bc965b7ddfe8075a0fcd732239cfff4","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The edge tab sits as a sibling at z-index 32, positioned absolutely relative to the app-shell with its left offset animating, staying above the main content. Now I'm writing the desktop media query to keep the sidebar fixed in place while the library frame slides over it...\n\nStill writing styles...\n\nI'm checking specificity concerns—making sure the media-query override for `.sidebar:not(.is-open)` wins since it comes later with equal specificity, and verifying the main-content transition covers both margin and padding. With z-index auto on the sidebar and main-content painting later in the DOM, main stays visually on top, and since the sidebar's background is transparent, the app background shows through the exposed corner correctly.\n\nI'm also checking whether the desktop sidebar z-index of 30 matters elsewhere, and whether hiding the closed sidebar with visibility also hides the docked mascot brand-mark—since the mascot likely roams away when the sidebar closes via an \"is-away\" state, this should be fine since position stays the same rather than shrinking as before.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YKAsdnBPQ6UeRGCEvkHHjm","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304\\src\\App.css","old_string":"  .sidebar {\n    border-right-color: transparent;\n    background: transparent;\n  }\n  .main-content {\n    --stage-background: var(--library-frame);","new_string":"  /* The sidebar holds still underneath and the library frame slides over it, so\n     only the frame's left edge moves. */\n  .sidebar,\n  .sidebar:not(.is-open) {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 0;\n    z-index: auto;\n    width: var(--sidebar-width);\n    padding: 26px 10px 6px;\n    border-right-color: transparent;\n    background: transparent;\n    opacity: 1;\n    transition: visibility 0s;\n  }\n  /* Hidden once covered, so its controls leave the tab order. */\n  .sidebar:not(.is-open) {\n    visibility: hidden;\n    transition: visibility 0s 0.3s;\n  }\n  .main-content {\n    margin-left: var(--sidebar-width);\n    transition:\n      margin-left 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1),\n      padding 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);\n  }\n  .sidebar:not(.is-open) ~ .main-content {\n    margin-left: 0;\n  }\n  .main-content {\n    --stage-background: var(--library-frame);"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
