{"parentUuid":"647ff2dc-a510-480c-8558-b6a5e944aece","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFNGuZN1tduebgd6nMqR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Mobile styles stay untouched since the changes are scoped to the min-width 781 block, and this is just a UI tweak so no changelog entry is needed. I'll leave the commit for the user to request as before, and I'll capture screenshots of both the open and mid-close states since the transition is the most telling part.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":564,"cache_read_input_tokens":86495,"output_tokens":597,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":113},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":564,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":597,"cache_read_input_tokens":86495,"cache_creation_input_tokens":564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":564},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":5606,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFNGu8aLXh56ES41Johj","requestRef":"408ae231-141b-4ac0-bda3-78042493662a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6f2e91c2-3957-461e-8517-16b22a5c88b1","timestamp":"2026-10-21T12:17:16.837Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"6f2e91c2-3957-461e-8517-16b22a5c88b1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFNGuZN1tduebgd6nMqR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Collapsing and opening the sidebar now works the way you described. The sidebar stays where it is, and the library frame slides left over it with its rounded corner, then slides back to uncover it. Nothing gets pushed to the left any more.\n\nI checked it in the Electron preview by slowing the slide down to grab a frame mid-close:\n\n![Sidebar mid-close, library frame sliding over it](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\sidebar-overlap\\2-mid-close.png)\n\n- **What changed:** only the desktop rules in `src/App.css`. On wide windows the sidebar keeps its full width and no longer fades, and the library frame's left edge animates instead. The edge tab already moved in step with the frame, so it still does. The narrow-window drawer is unchanged.\n- **Keyboard:** once the sidebar is fully covered, it's hidden from the tab order so its links can't be reached by keyboard while it's out of sight.\n- **Performance:** I measured six toggles in a row, several times each, with the old and new versions. The occasional slow frame shows up at about the same rate in both, so no regression. This doesn't fix the existing cost, though: the grid still reflows during the slide because the library really does change width.\n\nBiome passes on `App.css`. I ran the preview build and Electron on a scratch profile, then stopped them and restored the registry.\n\nThis isn't committed yet. Do you want it pushed to #170 like the last change?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":564,"cache_read_input_tokens":86495,"output_tokens":597,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":113},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_t