{"parentUuid":"f4ac85db-a64a-41ac-b505-f2c3ee7e53e1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFPbvmgUEXQpHFBi6Bod","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm reconsidering the blur strength and height ranges, and looking into why the window controls appear to have an opaque black background behind them in the screenshot—possibly from the sidebar-collapsed state rather than the controls CSS itself.\n\nI'm checking whether this black box matches the native titleBarOverlay region in main.mjs, and also wondering if the toolbar buttons and liquid glass elements are rendering under the blur layer due to z-index ordering between the blur and capture-bar components.\n\nActually I think I've found it: the liquid glass effect is drawn onto the stage canvas beneath the blur overlay, so the glass pill borders get blurred while the DOM icons/text on top stay sharp — that mismatch is the visual bug. A fix would mean moving the blur bands so they're part of the canvas content the glass refracts, or falling back to CSS backdrop-filter mode when WebGPU isn't available.\n\nI'm going to try placing the edge fade inside the LiquidGlass children, within the library stage after the scroll area, so the bands sit correctly in canvas mode — I need to check how the content wrapper inside LiquidGlass's canvas is structured first. The edge tab is also a liquid target to account for, and separately I still need to track down the black box issue with the window controls.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3235,"cache_read_input_tokens":133324,"output_tokens":1363,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1073},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3235,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"glo