{"parentUuid":"6432779d-b133-4dc6-a2ec-d69eee680788","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFPe1BeiJHuNYgrEC2oS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm realizing both the native overlay and React controls are rendering simultaneously, with the opaque native buttons showing on top. The fix is to drop titleBarOverlay entirely and rely solely on the custom transparent HTML controls with frame disabled and titleBarStyle hidden, so no native buttons appear at all.\n\nOne tradeoff: losing the native overlay also loses the Windows 11 snap layout flyout on maximize hover. Before fully removing it, I want to try setting the overlay color to a transparent rgba value and verify with an actual OS-level screenshot rather than a CDP capture, since CDP doesn't render native overlays.\n\nI'll lose the maximize-hover snap flyout but I'm leaning toward native transparent overlay. Let me test by setting the color to fully transparent and capturing a screenshot via PowerShell to check the result, then shift focus to the blur changes and move the blur into the stage, looking at the LiquidGlass structure for its children.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":470,"cache_read_input_tokens":140053,"output_tokens":1104,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":951},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":470,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1104,"cache_read_input_tokens":140053,"cache_creation_input_tokens":470,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":470},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thi