{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","prNumber":170,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Squidys-Tools/inkling/pull/170","prRepository":"Squidys-Tools/inkling","timestamp":"2026-10-21T12:45:40.329Z"}
{"parentUuid":"d89f5de1-2ff7-439d-8a4c-a6f629f30708","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFQSw2BUVt5Vn6HLdsw1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm realizing the gap is because those strips sit outside the scroller before my change, leaving them empty. The fix is to clip the library scroll to the old rect while an item is open, which means adding a state flag on main tied to whether selectedItem exists.\n\nI'm adding a `has-open-item` class to the main content and a corresponding clip-path rule using the scroll-reach variables, plus hiding the gradual blur elements since they're still descendants even when portaled into the canvas. I need to check what happens during the close flight—since selectedItem likely stays set until the flight finishes, the clip should persist and then drop away cleanly once it's cleared, so the strips only reappear after the overlay is gone.\n\nI'll just use CSS visibility hidden rather than display none for the blur so it doesn't force an unmount. The tint mask at top/bottom strips should be negligible but I'll hide it anyway for safety, and then apply the ref and className onto the main element.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":767,"cache_read_input_tokens":166282,"output_tokens":1419,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":668},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":767,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1419,"cache_read_input_tokens":166282,"cache_creation_input_tokens":767,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":767},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":12280,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFQSvc8C78NVw2XXbMJT","requestRef":"7de20cfa-137c-4e9e-b71f-ad7341ff51d0","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3e2c3f5e-cf27-402e-be4b-2b6418c6e52f","timestamp":"2026-10-21T12:45:53.430Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"3e2c3f5e-cf27-402e-be4b-2b6418c6e52f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFQSw2BUVt5Vn6HLdsw1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The item view is sized to the old library area, so the newly extended grid shows above and below it. I'm clipping the grid back to that area and hiding the edge blur while an item is open."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":767,"cache_read_input_tokens":166282,"output_tokens":1419,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":668},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":767,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1419,"cache_read_input_tokens":166282,"cache_creation_input_tokens":767,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":767},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgFQSvc8C78NVw2XXbMJT","requestRef":"7de20cfa-137c-4e9e-b71f-ad7341ff51d0","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7f558b5b-57ac-4f01-9c77-e8a058c69ea8","timestamp":"2026-10-21T12:45:53.433Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"7f558b5b-57ac-4f01-9c77-e8a058c69ea8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFQSw2BUVt5Vn6HLdsw1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H8eFnQjr9J2i4MNFCG2yrz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/App.tsx'; s=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nold='<main className=\"main-content\" ref={libraryFrameRef}>'\nnew='<main className={`main-content${selectedItem ? \" has-open-item\" : \"\"}`} ref={libraryFrameRef}>'\nassert s.count(old)==1; s=s.replace(old,new); open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\np='src/components/LibraryEdgeFade.tsx'; s=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ns=s.replace('  zIndex: 1,\\n};','  zIndex: 1,\\n  className: \"library-edge-blur\",\\n};')\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\np='src/App.css'; s=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nold='''.library-scroll.has-pinned-query .library-grid {\n  padding-top: calc(var(--scroll-reach-top) + 100px);\n}'''\nnew=old+'''\n/* The item view fills the frame inside its padding, so the grid's reach past\n   that padding would show above and below it. */\n.has-open-item .library-scroll {\n  clip-path: inset(var(--scroll-reach-top) 0 var(--scroll-reach-bottom));\n}\n.has-open-item .library-edge-blur {\n  visibility: hidden;\n}'''\nassert s.count(old)==1; s=s.replace(old,new); open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nEOF\ntimeout 60 bunx biome check --write src/App.tsx src/App.css src/components/LibraryEdgeFade.tsx 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Clip grid and hide edge blur while an item is open"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":767,"cache_read_input_tokens":166282,"output_tokens":1419,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":668},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":767,"ephemer