{"parentUuid":"b34a1487-7893-45f8-9cbe-08bff2abcd12","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_014MPwxQiESQMQwimrRZhy6f","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"2d36f069-5e87-49ac-a4a0-d652bf5d70d7","timestamp":"2026-10-21T12:47:39.709Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"2d36f069-5e87-49ac-a4a0-d652bf5d70d7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFQbLpdiCXL6hgdSigb1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Your React Bits settings are applied and the item view is clean now. Both are pushed to #170 as `7e997a5`.\n\n![Item view](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\sidebar-overlap\\8-item.png)\n\n- **Blur settings:** both edges now use what you picked: ease-in curve, strength 1, 8 layers, 4rem tall, and exponential on. Saturation, opacity and hover intensity are all 1, and auto hide is off. Smooth scroll was a setting for the demo page only, so there was nothing to apply.\n- **Tint:** our copy of the React Bits component takes a color but has no \"tint amount\", so I applied your 0.3 as transparency: `#120f17` at 30%. This adds a faint dark wash at the edges. You said earlier you didn't want a dark blur, but this is what you picked on the site, so I applied it as-is.\n- **Item view:** the item view covers the grid's old area, so the grid running past it showed at the top and bottom. While an item is open, the grid is now clipped back to its old area and the edge blur is hidden. They come back when you close it.\n\nThere's a small performance cost. Two blurred edges with 8 layers each dropped 1–5 single frames per scroll in my runs, compared with 0–1 at 5 layers. That's probably not noticeable, but going back to `layers: 5` in `src/components/LibraryEdgeFade.tsx` would remove most of it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":641,"cache_read_input_tokens":174910,"output_tokens":487,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":641,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations"