{"parentUuid":"446d2f01-c068-4621-974c-1aa2c012a685","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01DMSms2Bkf64hRFn8YJMt7i","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5cd16121-859f-474e-bb8b-efa1b942bc97","timestamp":"2026-10-21T12:50:58.221Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"5cd16121-859f-474e-bb8b-efa1b942bc97","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFQqxTeDjMtJCAHLnkrF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You can barely see a difference. Comparing the two screenshots pixel by pixel, the change stays within the top ~60px and bottom ~40px. The biggest color shift was 28 out of a possible 765.\n\n**Top edge**, 5 layers then 8:\n![5 layers top](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\sidebar-overlap\\layers-5-top.png)\n![8 layers top](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\sidebar-overlap\\layers-8-top.png)\n\n**Bottom edge**, 5 layers then 8:\n![5 layers bottom](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\sidebar-overlap\\layers-5-bottom.png)\n![8 layers bottom](C:\\Users\\chris\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\agents\\chat-images\\sidebar-overlap\\layers-8-bottom.png)\n\nThese are cropped from the same scroll position and enlarged 1.5×. More layers smooth out the fade itself, so it's the step from sharp to blurred that changes, not how strong the blur is.\n\nI also timed both with your current settings, three runs each. These are dropped frames out of about 310:\n\n| | Scroll | Sidebar slide |\n|---|---|---|\n| 5 layers | 2, 1, 0 | 20, 2, 0 |\n| 8 layers | 3, 2, 3 | 8, 14, 26 |\n\nThe runs vary a lot, but 8 layers comes out a bit worse overall, mainly on the sidebar slide.\n\nI'd go with 5, since it looks the same and runs a little smoother. The code is still on 8 (what's pushed); tell me which and I'll push it to #170."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":515,"cache_read_input_tokens":180575,"output_tokens":593,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":515,"epheme