{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","prNumber":170,"prUrl":"https://github.com/Squidys-Tools/inkling/pull/170","prRepository":"Squidys-Tools/inkling","timestamp":"2026-10-21T15:03:57.027Z"}
{"parentUuid":"012a9b68-c5f8-4792-951e-e4851b4a64de","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFazWBkJv7ZVf1LTu1hW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm planning the view-switching logic: the toggle indicator updates immediately, but if reduced motion is on or there are no cards, the list mode switches instantly, otherwise I fade out the current cards before transitioning.\n\nThen after the list mode state changes, I need the new cards to fade/pop in with a staggered delay based on their grid position (top-left to bottom-right), but since virtualization mounts cards asynchronously, I need to compute delays after mount via a rAF measurement rather than relying on static CSS delays.\n\nFor timing, I'll wait a couple of rAFs for Virtuoso's masonry layout to settle before running the GSAP stagger, since starting too early could use wrong positions -- though minor shifts during animation should still look acceptable. For list view, rows should pop in top-to-bottom with a similar staggered animation.\n\nI need to check whether the grid key changes with listMode and whether the masonry container persists across mode switches, since I'll target the grid element directly via a ref query. I'm deciding whether to fade individual cards or the whole grid element -- fading the grid itself is simpler, so I'm sequencing: add an entering class before paint, clear the opacity override, then wait a couple of frames before triggering the reveal.\n\nFor the stagger animation on visible cards, I'm animating from faded/scaled/offset states back to normal with an eased duration and index-based delay, then cleaning up the entering class and inline props on completion -- since the CSS class hides cards until removed, but inline opacity from the animation overrides that anyway, so offscreen cards stay hidden correctly until the class clears. Now I'm considering whether to animate the card slot wrapper or the inner card element itself, given virtualization renders each item through a slot container.\n\nI'm settling on targeting the card element directly since it has the rounded media, and noting that the glass canvas repainting during animation is fine, reduced motion should bypass to an instant switch, and scroll position resets aren't something I need to handle here.\n\nI also want to simplify the overly complex CSS selectors down to a simpler not-list-mode rule, strip out the now-unnecessary transition overlay div and its associated styles, and remove the view-transitioning class -- then double check the grid key logic and existing scroll-related gsap calls plus the toggle logic further down to make sure nothing conflicts.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4702,"cache_read_input_tokens":210953,"output_tokens":1912,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1627},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4702,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1912,"cache_read_input_tokens":210953,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4702,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4702},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":21746,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFazVpRaxGqjnAU7F3wn","requestRef":"78c7e162-fbf1-4f79-a8f0-c487e0343a17","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a77631e3-0fd0-4ebb-9942-ba506c2cb390","timestamp":"2026-10-21T15:04:19.519Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\i