{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","id":"d9db2da6-8e55-4562-b39b-8fcf99c53fc5","timestamp":"2026-10-21T15:04:19.686Z","version":"2.1.306","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"a9a28c5b6d177e7523d45bd1fa0389c337d1b62c694cec438d7585a7f2853a63","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"summarized"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"78c7e162-fbf1-4f79-a8f0-c487e0343a17","keep":413,"tail":["6a1b7a77ac5cf2092bf7184b0a818ec1b0ffcb12cb69d1105a5dbe488f08a2bf","e88a3699e337f6dd68a85a248d8569f868ffec4408ebdef8f191a9da29d967fb","d5970f0278b099fa0bea978242d66e6fc744b456055c18dd0aa5592a4f276042"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",415,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"06da367954c3edf6f8c3fe83e7bf87a0a3b157d1fb0a0ad1b49fbe97b260a8f0"}
{"parentUuid":"d714735a-efba-41c7-a049-fd4da0a59ae6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFb2BKzzHhmRhXiKysFr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm planning to remove unused helper code and replace the view-switching logic with a new implementation that fades out current cards, swaps the layout, then animates in the new view.\n\nI'm working through an edge case: if someone toggles the view rapidly mid-fade back to its original state, the completion callback could set listMode to a value that matches current state, meaning no layout effect fires and the grid gets stuck at zero opacity. I need to restructure the entrance logic as a reusable function triggered by a layout effect keyed on listMode, so partial transitions and rapid toggles resolve correctly instead of leaving the UI in a broken visual state.\n\nWriting entrance animation logic...\n\nFinishing the completion callback, then verifying that onInterrupt fires correctly in GSAP 3 when an animation is killed mid-flight, so I can reset classes and clear transform props reliably. I also need to make sure stale rAF calls from rapid toggling don't trigger animations after the state has already changed.\n\ncaptured value is stable since killed tweens don't fire onComplete. Now I'm worried the \"is-entering\" class approach for hiding cards during entrance won't survive React re-rendering className on the same grid element, since React would overwrite any classList changes I make imperatively. I should switch to a data attribute or state-driven class instead to avoid that conflict.\n\nI'm also checking that inline style props from VirtuosoMasonry won't accidentally clear opacity on re-render since React only diffs changed style keys, so that should be safe. Scroll position reset on view switch I'll leave alone for now, and I'm noting that filter changes remount the grid via its key.\n\nThe old scroll effect used gsap, so I need to keep that import, and the view toggle still uses viewSelectionListMode so that stays as is. On unmount I should kill the animation to clean up, and then I'll write the actual edits using line anchors.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2963,"cache_read_input_tokens":215655,"output_tokens":2752,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2503},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2963,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2752,"cache_read_input_tokens":215655,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2963,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2963},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":27445,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFb2Avw6jpJ29edRshZW","requestRef":"d9db2da6-8e55-4562-b39b-8fcf99c53fc5","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c01e1e26-f471-4189-aa3a-8fc5d21c2156","timestamp":"2026-10-21T15:04:47.920Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
