{"parentUuid":"289f8439-008a-42ed-aa82-afa0861276b2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a3517b34-cc8c-4b62-a00d-702b9173dc92","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E3iWSbQiXRP98gr1gn4qQx","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/changelog.md:50:- Inkling mascot engine vendored from the MIT-licensed bloub avatar project (framework-free SVG morph engine only, no Vue shell) with a Paper-derived ink-blot shape (`inkling-splash`), a React mascot component wired into the sidebar brand mark (slow drift live, gentle sway under reduced motion, notification pastille while background work runs, sad eyes on capture errors), a dev-only board at `?mascot`, and frozen-frame SVGs under `docs/assets/mascots/` (`src/components/mascot/`, `scripts/mascot-board.ts`)\ndocs/changelog.md:70:- Liquid glass in the desktop app: the library toolbar, search chip, collapsed sidebar tab and image zoom control refract what is behind them through WebGPU and Chromium's HTML-in-Canvas, and fall back to the CSS glass when either is unavailable (#170)\ndocs/changelog.md:82:- Library cards load remote images in CORS mode and the desktop app adds a CORS header to image responses, so the liquid glass canvas can draw them; no extra requests are made (#170)\ndocs/changelog.md:111:- Library grid and list views soften into a progressive blur at the top edge, under the search bar, and the bottom edge, down to the window's last pixel; both stay in place while scrolling (`src/components/LibraryEdgeFade.tsx`, `src/components/GradualBlur/`, `src/App.css`, `src/App.tsx`)\ndocs/changelog.md:153:- List view rows for notes, quotes, and videos sit in the same thumbnail column as other items, the quote text no longer overlaps itself, and the video play control sits on the thumbnail.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ba7e1e5b-fc44-44e5-963d-57beb2696ddb","timestamp":"2026-10-21T15:06:42.824Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"docs/changelog.md:50:- Inkling mascot engine vendored from the MIT-licensed bloub avatar project (framework-free SVG morph engine only, no Vue shell) with a Paper-derived ink-blot shape (`inkling-splash`), a React mascot component wired into the sidebar brand mark (slow drift live, gentle sway under reduced motion, notification pastille while background work runs, sad eyes on capture errors), a dev-only board at `?mascot`, and frozen-frame SVGs under `docs/assets/mascots/` (`src/components/mascot/`, `scripts/mascot-board.ts`)\ndocs/changelog.md:70:- Liquid glass in the desktop app: the library toolbar, search chip, collapsed sidebar tab and image zoom control refract what is behind them through WebGPU and Chromium's HTML-in-Canvas, and fall back to the CSS glass when either is unavailable (#170)\ndocs/changelog.md:82:- Library cards load remote images in CORS mode and the desktop app adds a CORS header to image responses, so the liquid glass canvas can draw them; no extra requests are made (#170)\ndocs/changelog.md:111:- Library grid and list views soften into a progressive blur at the top edge, under the search bar, and the bottom edge, down to the window's last pixel; both stay in place while scrolling (`src/components/LibraryEdgeFade.tsx`, `src/components/GradualBlur/`, `src/App.css`, `src/App.tsx`)\ndocs/changelog.md:153:- List view rows for notes, quotes, and videos sit in the same thumbnail column as other items, the quote text no longer overlaps itself, and the video play control sits on the thumbnail.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"289f8439-008a-42ed-aa82-afa0861276b2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
