{"parentUuid":"1a474e3a-507b-48d2-8a13-685e4e079296","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFfs9tWB5sbDMb6o73yB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"On desktop the sidebar toggle hides, with collapse handled by an edge tab, so I need somewhere for Add to live when collapsed. On mobile the sidebar becomes a drawer overlay with its toggle in the capture bar, so moving Add there would require opening the drawer just to add something—probably not ideal. Simplest solution: keep Add in the capture bar whenever the sidebar is closed, whether that's desktop-collapsed or mobile.\n\nI'm thinking a compact round + button could replace the toggle's position in the capture bar when the sidebar is closed, sitting at the left edge on both desktop and mobile; when the drawer is open on mobile, Add stays in the drawer footer instead.\n\nNow I need to figure out the view-controls positioning at the bottom center—since it's currently inside the capture-bar's flex layout, I'm considering pulling it out as a sibling element positioned absolutely relative to main-content instead, which means I need to check whether main-content has position: relative and how the library-stage and liquid glass rendering find their surfaces.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8449,"cache_read_input_tokens":96803,"output_tokens":926,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":611},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8449,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":926,"cache_read_input_tokens":96803,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8449,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8449},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"