{"parentUuid":"39dba4a9-e50f-49a5-ab27-802024227bbf","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01B38kBSa7MZ6GwoPBRP2de5","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5b53c66a-7767-4d1e-8820-c42db2609739","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:08:53.150Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
{"parentUuid":"5b53c66a-7767-4d1e-8820-c42db2609739","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFfuyVWZKSJDDrppWaCt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reallocating targets every time height changes is wasteful, so I should pad both bands to a shared max height to keep targets stable across frames, clamping so the band still fits within the canvas.\n\nFor rendering, I think I can render each band into a shared band texture, then copy it to the output per band via the encoder, submitting after each copy to guarantee ordering -- first copying the base content into output, then looping through bands to render and copy each at its top offset. I need to double check whether container.y changes require resyncing the source, since drawFrame may read glass positions at sync time rather than render time.\n\nI'm weighing whether to skip liquid glass for the bottom dock entirely and use a CSS backdrop-filter instead, but decide multi-band rendering keeps the look consistent. For computing bands, I'm figuring out margins, merging overlapping shape regions, rounding heights to a common step, clamping tops so bands fit within canvas bounds, and handling the case where padded bands overlap after height normalization -- reasoning that overlapping copies are harmless since the later band's correct render just overwrites the earlier one's rows.\n\nWriting band-merging logic...\n\nChecking the existing test cases against this new logic, I find one where the old behavior clipped height at the bottom but the new approach shifts the band upward to keep uniform height — that test needs updating. I should go look at the actual test file to confirm expected values, then also check the edge-tab behavior on desktop.\n\nWriting draw function logic...\n\nI also need to check whether container.y needs to be set before source.sync() runs, since the content range per glass might depend on it — I should grep the dist bundle for container.y usage in drawFrame to confirm the ordering.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1867,"cache_read_input_tokens":118059,"output_tokens":2249,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2063},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1867,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2249,"cache_read_input_tokens":118059,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1867,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1867},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":22729,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFfuyBAK8Le3kzn9CGBf","requestRef":"34c3d00c-5542-4d6d-881b-d972bacd1750","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"642b8323-7e99-42bc-8b26-303ffab88c19","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:08:53.150Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
