{"parentUuid":"ace63719-e369-44ad-94f6-01276e9e7ec5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"47279f09-bd61-46f5-88b0-75c11bf5f8f2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BNzdFuit9YTmZ3VEUpD3m8","type":"tool_result","content":"27:## Unreleased\n29:### Added\n72:### Fixed\n79:### Changed\n114:### Removed\n121:### Fixed\n158:## Phase 5 -- Reading and Writing (Aug 25, 2026)\n160:### Added\n168:## Phase 4 -- PDF, Embeddings, CI (Aug 17-18, 2026)\n172:### Added\n183:### Fixed\n192:## Phase 3 -- Background OCR (Aug 15, 2026)\ndocs/roadmap.md:84:- [x] Mascot that wanders the library on its own, drifting around the card grid and looking at things (SQU-58)\ndocs/changelog.md:66:- The mascot wanders the library on its own: 90 to 180 seconds after startup, and again after a long cooldown, it leaves the sidebar slot and drifts through the app, wearing a random expression at each stop and looking toward cards and recent pointer activity before going back. It never travels between points: it is given a direction and left to get on with it, with a turn rate that makes a change of mind a curve and a very small sway layered on the heading, so the path is unhurried, mostly straight and never the same twice. It never goes over the card grid - that is a wall it slides along rather than a filter on where it may stop - and the rest of the app, the sidebar and the strips of controls included, is somewhere it is allowed to be. It wanders in one part for a few seconds before it will consider blinking somewhere else, and it squashes out and swells up somewhere new and sets off again. It watches what the user does without being cancelled by it, holds still under overlays, dialogs, the expanded item, Serendipity and an in-flight drag, goes home sad when a capture fails, and never leaves home under reduced motion, plus a dev board at `?mascot-roam` (SQU-58) (`src/components/mascot/roam.ts`, `src/components/mascot/drift.ts`, `src/components/mascot/roamSpace.ts`, `src/components/mascot/roamStore.ts`)\ndocs/changelog.md:135:- The README mascot's body now moves exactly like the sidebar mascot's. It was running a separate copy of the sidebar drift with every period snapped to a divisor of 24 so the state would close on itself, which made the silhouette recur every 12s while the body took twice as long to come round. The loop never needed that — an SVG keyframe track already interpolates its last keyframe to the opening one — so both states now share one body (`inkling-drift-faced`) and the loop closes where it always was. The gaze wander stops being a second hand-rolled copy of `liveliness` for the same reason (`src/components/mascot/bot/states.ts`, `src/components/mascot/readmeMascot.ts`, `docs/assets/mascots/inkling-splash-loop.svg`)\ndocs/roadmap.md:84:- [x] Mascot that wanders the library on its own, drifting around the card grid and looking at things (SQU-58)\nsrc/components/mascot/faceMargin.test.ts:87:  if (look) engine.setLook({ ...look, mix: 1, spin: 0, wander: 0.35 }, -10);\n11\n48:export function prefersReducedMotion(): boolean {\n111:export function subscribeMascot(fn: () => void): () => void {\n126:export function onMascotClock(fn: (clock: number) => void): () => void {\n135:export function getMascotFrame(): BotFrame {\n164:export function pushMascotParams({ state, expression }: MascotParams) {\n170:export function pushRoamParams(params: MascotParams | null) {\n174:  if (!roamParams) engine.setLook(null, clock);\n179:export function pushMascotLook(look: Look | null) {\n180:  engine.setLook(look, clock);\n188:export function sampleMascotAt(t: number): BotFrame {\n197:export function LiveMascotFigure({\n215:export function LiveMascotSearchEyes({\nsrc/components/mascot/AliveBoard.tsx:110:        engine.setLook(\nsrc/components/mascot/AliveBoard.tsx:115:      onPointerLeave={() => engine.setLook(null, clockRef.current)}\nsrc/components/mascot/faceMargin.test.ts:87:  if (look) engine.setLook({ ...look, mix: 1, spin: 0, wander: 0.35 }, -10);\nsrc/components/mascot/InklingMascot.tsx:73:    if (look) created.setLook(heldLook(look), -10);\nsrc/components/mascot/InklingMascot.tsx:91:    if (lookYaw === undefined || lookPitch === undefined) engine.setLook(null, clockRef.current);\nsrc/components/mascot/InklingMascot.tsx:92:    else engine.setLook(heldLook({ yaw: lookYaw, pitch: lookPitch }), clockRef.current);\nsrc/components/mascot/mascotStore.tsx:174:  if (!roamParams) engine.setLook(null, clock);\nsrc/components/mascot/mascotStore.tsx:180:  engine.setLook(look, clock);\nsrc/components/mascot/readmeMascot.ts:179: * explains, and the wander reaches the engine through `setLook` with `mix: 1`,\nsrc/components/mascot/readmeMascot.ts:212:  engine.setLook({ yaw: g.yaw, pitch: g.pitch, mix: 1, spin: 0, wander: 0 }, -10);","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"39fc1da4-8ac0-437a-9271-7c910e8d52f0","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:11:32.399Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"27:## Unreleased\n29:### Added\n72:### Fixed\n79:### Changed\n114:### Removed\n121:### Fixed\n158:## Phase 5 -- Reading and Writing (Aug 25, 2026)\n160:### Added\n168:## Phase 4 -- PDF, Embeddings, CI (Aug 17-18, 2026)\n172:### Added\n183:### Fixed\n192:## Phase 3 -- Background OCR (Aug 15, 2026)\ndocs/roadmap.md:84:- [x] Mascot that wanders the library on its own, drifting around the card grid and looking at things (SQU-58)\ndocs/changelog.md:66:- The mascot wanders the library on its own: 90 to 180 seconds after startup, and again after a long cooldown, it leaves the sidebar slot and drifts through the app, wearing a random expression at each stop and looking toward cards and recent pointer activity before going back. It never travels between points: it is given a direction and left to get on with it, with a turn rate that makes a change of mind a curve and a very small sway layered on the heading, so the path is unhurried, mostly straight and never the same twice. It never goes over the card grid - that is a wall it slides along rather than a filter on where it may stop - and the rest of the app, the sidebar and the strips of controls included, is somewhere it is allowed to be. It wanders in one part for a few seconds before it will consider blinking somewhere else, and it squashes out and swells up somewhere new and sets off again. It watches what the user does without being cancelled by it, holds still under overlays, dialogs, the expanded item, Serendipity and an in-flight drag, goes home sad when a capture fails, and never leaves home under reduced motion, plus a dev board at `?mascot-roam` (SQU-58) (`src/components/mascot/roam.ts`, `src/components/mascot/drift.ts`, `src/components/mascot/roamSpace.ts`, `src/components/mascot/roamStore.ts`)\ndocs/changelog.md:135:- The README mascot's body now moves exactly like the sidebar mascot's. It was running a separate copy of the sidebar drift with every period snapped to a divisor of 24 so the state would close on itself, which made the silhouette recur every 12s while the body took twice as long to come round. The loop never needed that — an SVG keyframe track already interpolates its last keyframe to the opening one — so both states now share one body (`inkling-drift-faced`) and the loop closes where it always was. The gaze wander stops being a second hand-rolled copy of `liveliness` for the same reason (`src/components/mascot/bot/states.ts`, `src/components/mascot/readmeMascot.ts`, `docs/assets/mascots/inkling-splash-loop.svg`)\ndocs/roadmap.md:84:- [x] Mascot that wanders the library on its own, drifting around the card grid and looking at things (SQU-58)\nsrc/components/mascot/faceMargin.test.ts:87:  if (look) engine.setLook({ ...look, mix: 1, spin: 0, wander: 0.35 }, -10);\n11\n48:export function prefersReducedMotion(): boolean {\n111:export function subscribeMascot(fn: () => void): () => void {\n126:export function onMascotClock(fn: (clock: number) => void): () => void {\n135:export function getMascotFrame(): BotFrame {\n164:export function pushMascotParams({ state, expression }: MascotParams) {\n170:export function pushRoamParams(params: MascotParams | null) {\n174:  if (!roamParams) engine.setLook(null, clock);\n179:export function pushMascotLook(look: Look | null) {\n180:  engine.setLook(look, clock);\n188:export function sampleMascotAt(t: number): BotFrame {\n197:export function LiveMascotFigure({\n215:export function LiveMascotSearchEyes({\nsrc/components/mascot/AliveBoard.tsx:110:        engine.setLook(\nsrc/components/mascot/AliveBoard.tsx:115:      onPointerLeave={() => engine.setLook(null, clockRef.current)}\nsrc/components/mascot/faceMargin.test.ts:87:  if (look) engine.setLook({ ...look, mix: 1, spin: 0, wander: 0.35 }, -10);\nsrc/components/mascot/InklingMascot.tsx:73:    if (look) created.setLook(heldLook(look), -10);\nsrc/components/mascot/InklingMascot.tsx:91:    if (lookYaw === undefined || lookPitch === undefined) engine.setLook(null, clockRef.current);\nsrc/components/mascot/InklingMascot.tsx:92:    else engine.setLook(heldLook({ yaw: lookYaw, pitch: lookPitch }), clockRef.current);\nsrc/components/mascot/mascotStore.tsx:174:  if (!roamParams) engine.setLook(null, clock);\nsrc/components/mascot/mascotStore.tsx:180:  engine.setLook(look, clock);\nsrc/components/mascot/readmeMascot.ts:179: * explains, and the wander reaches the engine through `setLook` with `mix: 1`,\nsrc/components/mascot/readmeMascot.ts:212:  engine.setLook({ yaw: g.yaw, pitch: g.pitch, mix: 1, spin: 0, wander: 0 }, -10);","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ace63719-e369-44ad-94f6-01276e9e7ec5","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","version":"2.1.306","gitBranch":"feat/glass-surface","slug":"purrfect-munching-gadget"}
